  "problem": "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $123\\,321\\,87◻$ divisible by $4?$\n\nI. $2$\n\nII. $4$\n\nIII. $8$",
  "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $4$ if the last two digits form a number that is divisible by $4.$\n\nThe last two digits of the number $123\\,321\\,87◻$ are $7◻.$\n\n- If $2$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $72,$ which is indeed divisible by $4.$\n\n- If $4$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $74,$ which is *not* divisible by $4.$\n\n- If $8$ is substituted into the blank, then the last two digits are $78,$ which is *not* divisible by $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
